      "program_name": "Behavioral Health Services Act (BHSA) Integrated Plan FY 2026-27 through FY 2028-29, housing interventions",
      "administering_agency": "County of Santa Clara Behavioral Health Services Department (BHSD)",
      "funding_type": "other",
      "typical_award_size": "Total BHSA expenditure budget about $160 million a year; Housing Interventions component at the statutory 30 percent, $48 million a year (no transfer or exemption requested). Uses: tenant-based rental assistance for up to 700 individuals a year (500 permanent, 200 interim), continuation of the Casa de Novo interim housing program, Transitional Rent and Housing Deposits as a Medi-Cal managed care plan contracted provider from January 1, 2026, and licensed residential care facility support through a separate $8,038,653 CCE Preservation grant ($4,578,568 capital, $3,460,085 operating).",
      "per_unit_cap": "Not applicable. The plan funds no project-based units (units funded per year reported as 0).",
      "affordability_requirement": "BHSA-eligible adults with serious mental illness or substance use disorder who are homeless or at risk; 50 percent of housing funds targeted to chronically homeless individuals, with a focus on encampments.",
      "eligible_project_types": [
        "supportive housing",
        "interim housing",
        "services/operations"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "Draft Integrated Plan adopted by the Board June 2, 2026 and submitted to DHCS by June 30, 2026; plan period July 1, 2026 to June 30, 2029. Annual updates each spring.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "false",
      "layering_notes": "santaclaracounty.gov subdomains (osh, asr, bhsd, news, files) returned HTTP 403 to automated access on 2026-11-07; records were built from the Board of Supervisors IQM2 legislative files (sccgov.iqm2.com), the County Housing Element, Santa Clara County Housing Authority documents, HCD and BOE pages. Santa Clara County elected not to use BHSA for capital development (the plan says MHSA housing funds go to interventions that provide more immediate access) and not to fund operating subsidies with BHSA, so unlike San Diego or Sacramento there is no BHSA capital or PSH operating line to underwrite here. BHSD contracts with two providers for on-site specialty mental health services at PSH developments and will refer BHSA clients to County and SCCHA project-based units through coordinated entry. The Casa de Novo site (Homekey) continues as interim housing. Plan PDF: sccgov.iqm2.com/Citizens/FileOpen.aspx?Type=4&ID=270066 (Attachment B).",
